t · same envelope for every option</small></div></header>\n<main><section><div class=\"stage\"><div class=\"floating\" id=\"shapeBadge\">Hexagonal truncated pyramids</div><canvas id=\"view\" aria-label=\"Interactive 3D paper elephant\"></canvas><div id=\"error\">Your browser does not support WebGL. Open one of the included preview images instead.</div><div class=\"camera\"><button id=\"perspective\" class=\"active\">Perspective</button><button id=\"side\">Side</button><button id=\"front\">Front</button><button id=\"top\">Top</button><button id=\"reset\">Reset</button><div class=\"zoom-controls\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Model zoom\"><span>Zoom</span><button id=\"zoom-out\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button><button id=\"zoom-in\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button></div></div></div><p class=\"instructions\">Drag to rotate · Scroll to zoom · The assembly is shown at its calculated proportions.</p></section>\n<aside><h2>Choose your shape</h2><select id=\"shape\" aria-label=\"Shape option\"><option value=\"6\">Hexagonal truncated pyramids</option><option value=\"4\">Rectangular truncated pyramids</option><option value=\"3\">Triangular truncated pyramids</option></select><p id=\"description\"></p><div class=\"key\"><span id=\"solidCount\"></span><span>One solid type only</span></div><label for=\"part\">Inspect a body part</label><select id=\"part\"><option value=\"all\">Whole elephant</option></select><div class=\"row\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"edges\" checked> Show fold boundaries</label></div><label for=\"explode\">Separate the sections <span id=\"explosionLabel\">0%</span></label><input id=\"explode\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\"><div class=\"stat\" id=\"partInfo\"></div><a class=\"download\" id=\"obj\" download>Download this 3D model (.obj)</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"elephant-section-measurements.csv\" download>All section measurements (.csv)</a><button id=\"toggleDetails\" style=\"width:100%;margin-top:9px\">Show individual measurements</button><div id=\"pieceTable\" class=\"hidden\"></div></aside></main>\n<section class=\"section\"><h3>Where Fibonacci appears</h3><p class=\"intro\">The <strong>axial length</strong> of each section follows a scaled Fibonacci sequence. Cross-section widths and heights vary to shape the elephant. This updates the original base-width scheme: the progression now controls section lengths, not every dimension of the solid. Several body parts use shorter sequences; some run largest to smallest.</p><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Body part</th><th>Fibonacci terms, in assembly order</th><th>Section lengths (cm)</th><th>Total axial length</th></tr></thead><tbody id=\"schedule\"></tbody></table></div></section>\n<section class=\"section\"><h3>What the shape names mean</h3><p class=\"intro\">A truncated pyramid is a pyramid with its point cut off. Each section has two similar, parallel end faces joined by flat sides. The 3-sided option has triangular ends, the 4-sided option rectangular ends, and the 6-sided option hexagonal ends. Within each option, every modeled solid uses that same number of sides. Their proportions can differ; some are oblique, with the smaller end offset to bend the trunk or shape the body.</p><div class=\"notice\"><strong>Paper construction:</strong> these are hollow cardstock forms, not overlapping full pyramids. Adjacent sections within each body part share matching ends. Printed eyes are decoration, not additional solids. Small details and the ear-to-head attachments still need a physical assembly trial; the model is a construction prototype, not a tested commercial paper kit.</div></section><script>\nconst MODELS={\n  \"3\": {\n    \"sides\": 3,\n    \"pieces\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Body 1\",\n        \"part\": \"Body\",\n        \"group\": \"Body\",\n        \"vertices\": [\n          [\n            -2.625,\n            -0.945,\n            2.52\n          ],\n          [\n         